<title>GERMANY: D.Telekom sees doubling of parent net.</title>
<headline>D.Telekom sees doubling of parent net.</headline>
<dateline>HANOVER, Germany 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>German telecommunications giant Deutsche Telekom AG said on Tuesday it expects parent net profit to double this year from a preliminary 1.6 billion marks in 1996.</p>
<p>Telekom chairman Ron Sommer told reporters ahead of the CeBIT information technology trade fair that in order to pay a dividend of 1.20 marks as planned this year &quot;that we have a result in the parent company that is at least a doubling of the previous year.&quot;</p>
</text>
